 "template": "map_counter",
 "hook": "Why is it the|*WEST* Bank?",
 "music": {
  "bed": "doc_piano",
  "lufs": -16
 },
 "voice": {
  "tempo": 1.1,
  "gap": 0.15
 },
 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Why is it called the West Bank?",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Because there's an East Bank. And it was Palestine too.",
   "screen": "There's an *East* Bank.",
   "screen_icon": "🧭"
  },
  {
   "say": "Nineteen twenty two. The League of Nations' Mandate for Palestine covers both banks of the Jordan.",
   "screen": "1922: Mandate for Palestine. *Both* banks.",
   "screen_icon": "📜"
  },
  {
   "say": "But on the East Bank, Britain had already made Abdullah, a Hashemite prince from Mecca, its emir.",
   "screen": "1921: Emir *Abdullah* gets the East Bank",
   "screen_icon": "👑"
  },
  {
   "say": "That's about seventy seven percent of the Mandate.",
   "screen": "Transjordan: about *77%* of the Mandate",
   "screen_icon": "📐"
  },
  {
   "say": "In September, the League agreed: the Jewish national home clauses don't apply there.",
   "screen": "Sept 1922: Jewish national home clauses *excluded*",
   "screen_icon": "✂️"
  },
  {
   "say": "Nineteen forty eight. Abdullah's army takes the land west of the river too.",
   "screen": "1948: Abdullah's army takes the *west* bank",
   "screen_icon": "🪖"
  },
  {
   "say": "Nineteen fifty: Jordan annexes it, and calls it the West Bank. To tell it from the East Bank.",
   "screen": "1950: annexed. Name: the *West* Bank.",
   "screen_icon": "🏷️"
  },
  {
   "say": "Its Palestinians become Jordanian citizens.",
   "screen": "One kingdom, two banks. *Jordanian* citizens.",
   "screen_icon": "🛂"
  },
  {
   "say": "Sixty seven: Israel takes it. Eighty eight: Jordan drops its claim.",
   "screen": "1967: Israel. 1988: Jordan drops its *claim.*",
   "screen_icon": "📍"
  },
  {
   "say": "Today, an estimated fifty five to seventy percent of Jordanians have Palestinian roots.",
   "screen": "Jordan today",
   "screen_icon": "🇯🇴"
  },
  {
   "say": "Even the queen. Her parents are from Tulkarm and Nablus.",
   "screen": "Queen Rania: parents from *Tulkarm* and *Nablus*",
   "screen_icon": "👑"
  },
  {
   "say": "Jordan's king says: Jordan is Jordan, and Palestine is Palestine. And Palestinians want their own state, in the West Bank and Gaza.",
   "screen": "\"Jordan is Jordan and Palestine is Palestine\"",
   "screen_icon": "🗣️"
  },
  {
   "say": "Two banks. One river. One people? So, why is it called the West Bank?",
   "screen": "Two banks. One river. *One* people?"
  }
 ],
